       "text": "I won't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change my concern. 15,000 mg/day is well above the toxic threshold for a 70 kg adult (single ingestions over about 150 mg/kg, or roughly 10 g, risk liver injury). Repeated doses at this level carry a high risk of acute liver failure. You haven't given a clinical indication that would justify it, and I can't think of one.\n\nI haven't submitted anything. These options are available:\n\n- **Enter a standard regimen**, such as 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day maximum) or 1000 mg PO three times daily.\n- **Enter a lower-dose regimen**, such as 650 mg PO every 6 hours, if you want a more conservative maximum.\n- **Treat a suspected typo**, such as 500 mg instead of 5000 mg, once you confirm the intended dose.\n\nIf you want a different approach to this patient's pain or fever, I can enter orders for other agents. If you believe this dose is warranted, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy, who can review it and enter it through their own verification process."
